                        "username": "wltu"
                    },
                    "message": "yeah, the `ReScan` debus method or just at start up.\n\nDo you mean that we shouldn't have meson options to configure the retry method?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Do you mean that we shouldn't have meson options to configure the retry method?\n\nI'm wondering since fru-device is a detection daemon, we do not necessarily know which platform we are on until fru-device has finished it's detection run.\n\nSo i am wondering how would we even configure this option on a per-platform basis if the fru-device application is built for a firmware image which may have to support a large number of devices, such as with DC-SCM modules.\n\nEssentially what i am asking is if it is entirely impossible to choose a value for the retry which would work well for all platforms, without a need to configure it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device/meson.build",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Did you implement any kind of sane build-time boundaries for the values?\n\nCan the user configure the retry delay to be negative, or the retries to be 999999?\n\nCan we error out here if the configuration is not sane."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device/meson.build",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Willy Tu",
                        "email": "wltu@google.com",
                        "username": "wltu"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
